# Clipboard Viewer: the keys of arch311-ref/scn/clipbrd-bmp.scn (tools/ref311/scenario.py w16)
# Opens SYSTEM\CBBMP.CLP (mkclp.py: a VGA planar bitmap, a 4-bit DIB, a 22-entry palette), shows
# each format, saves BMP.CLP. The Open/Save As dialogs are commdlg.c's (not compared here).
# compare: clipbrd-bmp/01.png 01.png ignore 320 240 333 261
# compare: clipbrd-bmp/04.png 03.png ignore 320 240 333 261
# compare: clipbrd-bmp/05.png 04.png ignore 320 240 333 261
# compare: clipbrd-bmp/06.png 05.png ignore 320 240 333 261
# compare: clipbrd-bmp/07.png 06.png ignore 320 240 333 261
# compare: clipbrd-bmp/09.png 07.png ignore 320 240 333 261
# file: files/bmp.clp run-clipbrd-bmp/WINDOWS/BMP.CLP apps/clipbrd/tests/clpcmp.py
# regress: sh apps/clipbrd/tests/run.sh "$TEST" "$OUT"
sleep 400
sleep 400
shot shots/01.png
key alt
key f
key o
sleep 400
shot shots/02.png
key s
key y
key s
key t
key e
key m
key backslash
key c
key b
key b
key m
key p
key period
key c
key l
key p
key enter
sleep 400
shot shots/03.png
key alt
key d
sleep 400
shot shots/04.png
key d
sleep 400
shot shots/05.png
key alt
key d
key e
sleep 400
shot shots/06.png
key alt
key f
key a
key b
key m
key p
key period
key c
key l
key p
key enter
sleep 400
shot shots/07.png
quit
